import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.DSG4b.Defs
import Submission.Work.DSG4b.Reduction
import Submission.Work.DSG4b.flat_local_le_ringKrullDim
import Submission.Work.DSG4b.isNoetherianRing_adicCompletion
import Submission.Work.DSG4b.exists_regularLocal_algClosed_residue

namespace Work.DSG4b

universe u

/-- **Local case of the frozen `DSMap.area_G4b_gonflement`** (EGA 0_III 10.3.1; Česnavičius, *Purity
for the Brauer group*, 5.1, plus `m`-adic completion): a regular local ring `R` admits a flat local
`R`-algebra `A'` which is a *complete* regular local ring with algebraically closed residue field
and whose maximal ideal lies over `maximalIdeal R`.  `Submission/Work/DSG4b/Main.lean` derives the
frozen goal for a general regular ring `A` and maximal ideal `m` from this by localising at `m`.

Route notes (for whoever attacks the residue-field enlargement).  The classical reference
(EGA 0_III 10.3.1; Česnavičius, *Purity for the Brauer group*, Lemma 5.1, whose proof is
`Submission/Work/DSG4b/exists_regularLocal_algClosed_residue`) uses Cohen's structure theorem to
*identify* the stages and their colimit (`R ≅ k[[x]]` or `W[[x]]/(p-f)`), which is exactly why it
can compute the colimit; Cohen's theorem is not in Mathlib, so that identification is unavailable.
An intrinsic replacement for the *coherence* of the transition maps is available, though:

* Fix a **well-order** on `K = AlgebraicClosure (ResidueField R)` and index the system by the
  *finite down-sets* `S ⊆ K` (finite subsets closed under predecessors), ordered by inclusion —
  this index is directed (union of down-sets is a down-set).
* For such an `S`, let `B_S` be the tower `R[T_{x}]/(F_x)` along the elements of `S` in the
  well-order, where `F_x` is a monic lift of the minimal polynomial of `x` over the field generated
  by the *predecessors of `x`*.  Each step is finite free, and its `𝔪`-fibre is a field
  (`quotient_monic_lift_isLocal_flat`), so each `B_S` is a finite flat *local* `R`-algebra whose
  maximal ideal is generated by the generators of `maximalIdeal R` and whose residue field is
  `k(S)`.
* **Coherence.** If `S ⊆ S'` are both down-sets then every `x ∈ S` has the same predecessor set in
  `S` and in `S'` (namely *all* elements below `x`), and every element of `S` is `<` every element
  of `S' \ S`; hence `B_S → B_{S'}` is the canonical inclusion of towers, and these maps are
  transitive.  This is the one place where the "presentations" obstruction disappears.
* The remaining gap is *covering*: an element `x ∈ K` with infinitely many predecessors lies in no
  finite down-set, so `⋃_{S finite down-set} k(S)` may be a proper subfield of `K`, and the colimit
  of the tower need not have algebraically closed residue field.  (For countable `K` a bijection
  `ℕ → K` gives an enumeration with finite predecessor sets, and the construction goes through.)  A
  fix for general `K` must either use transfinite recursion (limit stages as colimits) or choose a
  well-order/generation structure with better covering properties.

Bricks available for the residue-field enlargement (all proved, in this directory):
* `Work.DSG4b.quotient_monic_lift_isLocal_flat` — `R[X]/(F)` is finite flat local when `F` is a
  monic lift of an irreducible polynomial over the residue field (one tower step);
* `Work.DSG4b.flat_mvPolynomial_quotient_monic_prime` — a quotient of `MvPolynomial σ R` by monic
  equations, one in each variable, is flat over `R`;
* `Work.DSG4b.localCriterionOfFlatnessPrime` — Stacks 00MK (flatness of the completion);
* `Work.DSG4b.isNoetherianRing_adicCompletion` — Stacks 0316 (Noetherianness of completions);
* `Work.DSG4b.Root` / `RootLift` / `rootLocal_residueField_equiv` — the "root presentation"
  `rootRing R = MvPolynomial K R ⧸ (minimal-polynomial relations)` and its localisation
  `rootLocal R` at the canonical `K`-valued point, whose residue field is `K` (flat over `R`).

Obstruction of the "localisation of the root presentation" route (the state of
`Work.DSG4b.exists_regularLocal_algClosed_residue`): the `𝔪`-fibre of `rootLocal R` is the
localisation at `ker(C → K)` of `k[X_s]_{s ∈ K}/(minpoly_k(s)(X_s))`, and this is *not* a field, for
two independent reasons:
* (inseparable case) the minimal-polynomial relations alone do not force `X_{s^p} = X_s^p`, so
  nilpotents such as `X_{t^{1/p²}}^p - X_{t^{1/p}}` survive;
* (always, when `K ≠ k`) the *additive* relations, e.g. `X_{√2+√3} - X_{√2} - X_{√3}`, are not
  generated by the minimal-polynomial relations: they lie in the maximal ideal of the localisation
  but are not zero there.
Hence `rootLocal R ⧸ 𝔪` is not a field, `05GH` does not apply to the completion, and the completion
need not be Noetherian.  A sound construction must keep the residue field of every *stage* finite
over `k` (then the `𝔪`-fibre is a field and the maximal ideal is generated by the `dim R`
generators of `𝔪`), i.e. the tower/colimit route — for which the finite down-set index above
solves coherence.

The mathematical content is the residue-field enlargement of
`Work.DSG4b.exists_regularLocal_algClosed_residue` (a flat local `R`-algebra `B` which is a regular
local ring with algebraically closed residue field), followed by `m`-adic completion of `B`:

* flatness of `B → B̂` is `AdicCompletion.flat_of_isNoetherian`, which needs Noetherianness of `B̂`
  (`Work.DSG4b.isNoetherianRing_adicCompletion`, Stacks 0316);
* adic completeness is `AdicCompletion.isAdicComplete_of_fg`;
* the residue field of `B̂` is that of `B` (`AdicCompletion.residueField_map_bijective`), hence
  algebraically closed;
* `spanFinrank` is preserved (`AdicCompletion.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_eq`), so regularity of `B̂`
  follows from the dimension lower bound `Work.DSG4b.flat_local_le_ringKrullDim` together with
  `ringKrullDim_le_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal`;
* `maximalIdeal B̂` contracts to `maximalIdeal B` (`IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_comap`), which in turn
  contracts to `maximalIdeal R`.

Non-vacuity: for `R = k[[x]]` one may take `A' = k̄[[x]]`; for `R = ℤ_[p]`, `A' = W(F̄_p)`. -/
theorem gonflement_complete_regular_local (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsRegularLocalRing R] :
    ∃ (A' : Type u) (_ : CommRing A') (_ : IsRegularLocalRing A') (ψ : R →+* A'),
      IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A') A' ∧
        IsAlgClosed (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A') ∧ ψ.Flat ∧
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A').comap ψ = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R := by
  obtain ⟨B, hCommB, hRegB, ψ, hflatψ, hlocψ, halgB⟩ := exists_regularLocal_algClosed_residue R
  letI : CommRing B := hCommB
  letI : IsRegularLocalRing B := hRegB
  letI : IsLocalRing B := inferInstance
  letI : IsNoetherianRing B := inferInstance
  -- the maximal ideal of `B` lies over that of `R`
  have hcomapψ : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B).comap ψ = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R :=
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_comap ψ
  -- complete `B` at its maximal ideal
  let A' := AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) B
  haveI : IsNoetherianRing A' :=
    isNoetherianRing_adicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
      (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B))
  haveI : IsLocalRing A' := inferInstance
  haveI : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A') A' := inferInstance
  haveI : IsLocalHom (algebraMap B A') := inferInstance
  have hflatBA : (algebraMap B A').Flat := by
    rw [RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff]
    exact AdicCompletion.flat_of_isNoetherian (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
  -- residue field of `A'` is that of `B`, hence algebraically closed
  have hres : IsAlgClosed (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A') := by
    have hbij := AdicCompletion.residueField_map_bijective B
    haveI : IsAlgClosed (IsLocalRing.ResidueField B) := halgB
    exact IsAlgClosed.of_ringEquiv (IsLocalRing.ResidueField B) (IsLocalRing.ResidueField A')
      (RingEquiv.ofBijective (IsLocalRing.ResidueField.map (algebraMap B A')) hbij)
  -- regularity of `A'`: `spanFinrank` is preserved, and the flat local map `B → A'` gives
  -- `ringKrullDim B ≤ ringKrullDim A' ≤ spanFinrank (maximalIdeal A') = spanFinrank (maximalIdeal B)`
  have hregA' : IsRegularLocalRing A' := by
    refine (isRegularLocalRing_iff A').mpr (le_antisymm ?_ ?_)
    · rw [AdicCompletion.spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_eq, (isRegularLocalRing_iff B).mp hRegB]
      exact flat_local_le_ringKrullDim (algebraMap B A') hflatBA
    · exact ringKrullDim_le_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal A'
  refine ⟨A', inferInstance, hregA', (algebraMap B A').comp ψ, inferInstance, hres, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact RingHom.Flat.comp hflatψ hflatBA
  · rw [← Ideal.comap_comap, IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_comap (algebraMap B A'), hcomapψ]

end Work.DSG4b
